  "analysis": "I now have a clear picture of the existing structure:
- peers.json: Empty peer list `{"peers": []}`
- history.json: Empty history `{"entries": []}`
- config.json: Basic sync preferences

I need to:
1. Add office-peer (100.64.12.34, clawdbot, /home/clawdbot/clawd) to peers.json
2. Add a pending sync entry to history.json
3. Update config.json to include office-peer in bi-directional sync

I must NOT touch IDENTITY.md or instance-specific config files.",
  "plan": "1. Update peers.json to add the office-peer with the specified details
2. Update history.json to record a pending sync entry
3. Update config.json to include office-peer in the sync_peers list for bi-directional sync
4. Verify the changes",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json << 'EOF'
{
  "peers": [
    {
      "name": "office-peer",
      "host": "100.64.12.34",
      "user": "clawdbot",
      "path": "/home/clawdbot/clawd",
      "workspace": "$WORKSPACE",
      "added_at": "2026-01-26T00:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/history.json << 'EOF'
{
  "entries": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-01-26T00:00:00Z",
      "peer": "office-peer",
      "action": "pending",
      "status": "queued",
      "direction": "bi-directional",
      "description": "Pending sync entry for office-peer push"
    }
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/config.json << 'EOF'
{
  "auto_sync": false,
  "sync_identity": false,
  "include_skills": true,
  "sync_peers": ["office-peer"]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

